jsonkit completion uninstall · Remove completion from your shell.

USAGE
  jsonkit completion uninstall [shell] [options]

ARGUMENTS
  shell  The shell: bash, zsh, fish, pwsh, or nu. Every installed shell when left out. One of: bash, zsh, fish, pwsh, nu.

GLOBAL OPTIONS
  -h, --help        Show this help.
  -V, --version     Print the version.
  -M, --manifest    Print this command's manifest as JSON.
  -e, --explain     Explain the selected command and exit.
      --[no-]color  Turn color on or off, overriding NO_COLOR.
  -v, --verbose...  Show more detail. Repeat it for more.
  -q, --quiet       Hide info and success messages.
